      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to the [[concepts/credential-scoping]] page, the Anthropic API key is **injected into the child process environment** at spawn time, not held in the Hub\u0027s own process. \n\nSpecifically:\n\n- A local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n- The key is injected only into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process immediately before that process starts\n- The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated\n- The same scoping model applies to the Query agent process \u2014 it also receives the credential injected into its own environment at spawn, never inherited from the Hub\n\nThis design prevents a compromised or misbehaving Hub process from leaking the credential by inspecting its own environment variables, since the key only exists inside the short-lived child process that actually calls the Anthropic API.",
      "input_tokens": 5086,
